NOTICE — the text in this directory is not ours
===============================================

The .tex files under transcripts/ are transcriptions of the Edward and
Josephine Hopper artist's ledgers, Whitney Museum of American Art, 96.208 to
96.213, made from the sheets the Whitney has digitised and published.

    (c) Heirs of Josephine N. Hopper, licensed by Artists Rights Society
    (ARS), New York.

    The Whitney records the object rights as transferred to the Museum.

A transcription reproduces Josephine Hopper's text. Josephine Hopper died in
1968, so that text is in copyright in the United States and in the European
Union for some years yet. No permission to reproduce it has been sought from
ARS or from anyone else, and none has been granted. These files are
unauthorised working documents, and every one of them says so on its own face:
the rights line is printed in the title block of each rendered file and
repeated as a watermark on every page of each PDF, and `npm run render` will
not build a file that omits it.

The repository's LICENSE dedicates the maintainers' own work to the public
domain under CC0. It does not, and cannot, reach the text in this directory.


What in these files IS ours
---------------------------

The .tex files are mixed. The apparatus around the transcribed text is the
maintainers' own work and is CC0 with the rest of the repository:

    \note{}          the transcriber's observations on a leaf
    \marginal{}      the description of what stands in the margins
    \keywords{}      the tags
    \hand{}          the attribution -- the choice of whose hand it is
    \uncertain{}     the marking of a doubtful reading
    the LaTeX structure, the section headings, and transcripts/preamble/

What is not ours is what the Hoppers wrote: the bodies of \hand{} and \work{},
and the quoted matter inside the ruled tables.


Facts are not covered by any of this
------------------------------------

Prices, dates, dimensions, buyers' names and accession numbers are facts, and
facts are not subject to copyright. The derived files under src/content/ —
works.json, accounts.json, formats.json, materials.json and the rest — are the
maintainers' own compilations of those facts and are CC0 without qualification.


